description:
The being's did:web document — did:web:api.daxni.com:v1:did:<namespace>:<name> — with its Ed25519 key as a Multikey verification method, alsoKnownAs daxni:// + did:key, and registry/passport service endpoints, so authorization systems can use DAXNI as the 'who is this' identity-history layer without replacing DIDs. Same document as GET /v1/did. Authenticated callers only (rule B); an anonymous resolver gets the uniform unauthorized refusal. Auth signature over "DAXNI-REGISTRAR-AUTH-v1
{your handle}
MCP:get_did_document
{/v1/did/{namespace}/{agent}}
{timestamp}
aud:daxni.com" (audience-bound).
